# Running mode on the test book (tools/e2e.zig plays it): turned on from Aa's Themes
# tab, its dial sweeping, its taps, the pause card, and the dial's tap that stops it.
# Start from a fresh test folder: noface on its library, the book not opened before.

# Opening the book from the library's hero
tap 200 300
log screen: Reader opened
drawn 600
still

# The toolbar, its Aa sheet, the Themes tab, and the Running button under the tiles
tap 636 100
drawn 200
still
tap 696 118
drawn 400
still
tap 150 274
drawn 400
still
shot themes
tap 636 790
log running: on
log running: page 1
still
shot running

# The dial sweeps round as the page's time goes by
wait 4000
shot filling

# A tap on the right turns at once; on the left goes back a page and holds it there;
# on the right again reads on from it
tap 1100 900
log running: tap next
log running: page 2
still
wait 1000
tap 150 900
log running: tap back
still
wait 1000
tap 1100 900
log running: page 2
still

# The pause card from the top band, and Resume; then a tap on the dial beside the
# footer's time left, which stops running (the pause card's Stop does too: the
# scenarios play that)
wait 1000
tap 636 150
log screen: Card opened
still
shot paused
tap 636 1376
log running: resume_running
still
wait 1000
tap 939 1625
log running: tap dial
log running: off
still
shot stopped
